==============================================================================
SECTION 2 - blitzy-curl PROJECT LICENSING POSITION
==============================================================================

Upstream copyright attribution
------------------------------

curl and libcurl are the work of Daniel Stenberg, <daniel@haxx.se>, and many
contributors, as recorded in the notice in Section 1 and in the upstream
THANKS file. Those copyright holders retain their copyright in the material
this project derives from. That attribution is retained here, in the notice
reproduced above, and in the project's own files that carry it.

Derivative work
---------------

The Rust implementation under refactor/ and the verification code under
testing/ are a derivative work of curl. They were written against curl's
source, public headers, documentation and tests, and they reproduce curl's
interfaces and behavior.

This project is NOT a clean-room reimplementation of curl, and it must not be
presented as one.

License applied to this project's own work
------------------------------------------

Everything this project authors - the whole of refactor/ and testing/, and
the root-level build, packaging and CI files - is licensed under the curl
license reproduced in Section 1. Its SPDX license identifier is curl.

No additional license is applied to this project's own work. Should an
additional license ever be applied, it is carried alongside the curl license
and never in place of it, and it is named in this file, in the root LICENSE
file and in refactor/COPYING.

Preserved baseline license
--------------------------

original/ is an unmodified vendored copy of upstream curl and is read-only.
The license files and license metadata of that tree are preserved there
exactly as upstream ships them:

  original/COPYING
  original/REUSE.toml
  original/LICENSES/curl.txt
  original/LICENSES/ISC.txt
  original/LICENSES/BSD-4-Clause-UC.txt

original/COPYING is upstream's root curl notice for that tree, and it is not
the license of every file in it. Upstream annotates licensing per file: an
SPDX-License-Identifier and SPDX-FileCopyrightText in the file itself where
the format allows one, and an entry in original/REUSE.toml where it does not.
Those per-file annotations, together with the license texts under
original/LICENSES/ - which include ISC and BSD-4-Clause-UC as well as curl -
govern the files they apply to, and they take precedence over the root notice
wherever the two differ.

Nothing in this file modifies, supersedes, replaces, reinterprets or restates
the terms of original/COPYING, of original/REUSE.toml, or of any file under
original/LICENSES/, and this file grants nothing in respect of that tree.

Companion files
---------------

The root LICENSE file is a duplicate of this file under the name that tooling
commonly expects; the two carry one license position and are changed
together.

refactor/COPYING and refactor/LICENSE state this same position for the Rust
implementation tree and do not vary it.

Where "why" is recorded
-----------------------

The rationale for this licensing position is recorded in
refactor/docs/DECISION-LOG.md, the project's single source of truth for "why"
decisions. It is not restated here.
